# Code owners for the files that carry the guards (zero-debt kit, 04-guards.md C4, point 22).
#
# Why: the override tag [ratchet: <name>] goes in a commit message, and the author of a pull request writes the commit messages.
# Nothing in the pipeline can tell a tag written for a real reason from one written to get past a guard; a review by the owner of
# these files can. Every file the guards, the caps and the pipeline live in is listed here, and the file lists itself, so a pull
# request cannot drop its own review by editing it. The last matching rule wins: a later rule must not name fewer owners.
#
# Enforcement: the repository is public, so branch protection can require a review from the code owners on `main`; that is a host
# setting the owner turns on in GitHub. The contract test reads this file and its rules; it cannot read the host setting.

# The scripts: the ratchet script and its table, the dashboard, the checks script, kit-config.sh, the commit-message check,
# the audit gate, the caps file, the floors, prepush.sh, mutation.sh.
/scripts/ @NiekNijland

# The pipeline: the workflow directory as a whole, and the dependency bot that moves its pins.
/.github/workflows/ @NiekNijland
/.github/dependabot.yml @NiekNijland

# The guards: the detector classes, the thin tests of the Guards suite, and phpunit.xml, which defines that suite.
/tests/Support/Architecture/ @NiekNijland
/tests/Guards/ @NiekNijland
/phpunit.xml @NiekNijland

# The format commits that blame skips.
/.git-blame-ignore-revs @NiekNijland

# This file itself.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @NiekNijland
